---
title: What's Next
description: Further resources for configuring feature flags in the Vonage Video Android App.
---

Congratulations, you have successfully completed the tutorial! Copy the public VERA backend server URL from this Codespace and paste it into the learning path to generate your certificate of completion — you don't need to keep this Codespace open or the server running afterwards.

## What You Accomplished

- Started the shared backend server in this Codespace and made its port public
- Cloned `vonage-video-android-app` to your own machine, pointed it at the backend via `local.properties`, and ran the app
- Understood the structure of `config/app-config.json`, including its `videoSettings`, `audioSettings`, `waitingRoomSettings`, and `meetingRoomSettings` sections
- Edited feature flags in `app-config.json` and regenerated `AppConfig.kt` and `gradle/generated-config.properties` with `./gradlew generateVonageConfig`
- Rebuilt the app and confirmed your changes on an emulator or device

## What's Next

Want to also customize the app's colors, typography, and shape? Continue with the companion **Vonage Video Android App Theme Customization** tutorial — it picks up from the same local setup and walks through `config/theme.json`.

